Subject: [PATCH] net: ppe: check FDB upper type before bridge VLAN access

A topology transition may leave a non-bridge upper device in a cached
flow. Check its type before br_vlan_enabled() reads bridge private state.
Keep the existing RTNL, flow lock and RCU lifetime ordering.

Carried from the RC01 adjustment in 1f23a593fcbf775a849c7cb9f3709f8a899d7c99;
upstream moved the worker from local 0681 into 0680 during regrouping.
Renumbered from local 0686 after the upstream 0686-0694 PPE series, which
does not add this check.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -4997,7 +4997,8 @@
 			continue;
 		rcu_read_lock();
 		master = netdev_master_upper_dev_get_rcu(idev);
-		vid = master && br_vlan_enabled(master) ?
+		vid = master && netif_is_bridge_master(master) &&
+			br_vlan_enabled(master) ?
 			(flow->vlan >= 0 ? ft->vlans[flow->vlan].cvid :
 			 flow->rule.data.ingress_cvid) : 0;
 		valid = master && netif_is_bridge_master(master) &&
